{
  "reconstructed": true,
  "scheme": {
    "timestamp_header": "X-Robert-Timestamp",
    "signature_header": "X-Robert-Signature",
    "message": "<X-Robert-Timestamp>.<raw body>: the timestamp header's value, a period, and the request body exactly as it arrived, before any JSON parsing.",
    "mac": "HMAC-SHA256",
    "key": "The event's webhook secret as UTF-8 bytes. Robert issues it when the webhook URL is set (api.json, set_webhook_url), and pixl's comment says it starts with whsec_.",
    "signature_format": "sha256= followed by the 64 lowercase hex digits of the MAC.",
    "timestamp_format": "Unix time in whole seconds, as decimal digits.",
    "tolerance_s": 300,
    "receiver_rule": [
      "Refuse when either header is missing. Carnival and Alchemize also refuse outright when the secret is empty.",
      "Refuse unless X-Robert-Timestamp is one or more ASCII digits.",
      "Refuse when the timestamp is more than 300 s from the receiver's clock, either way. The clock has fractions (Date.now() / 1000), so 300.5 s off is refused and exactly 300 s is accepted.",
      "Compute sha256= and the hex MAC, and compare that with X-Robert-Signature byte for byte in constant time. A different length, uppercase hex or a missing prefix fails.",
      "Parse the body only after it verifies."
    ],
